    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CDC:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " after travel to Iraq or Pakistan, or with no international travel, treat complicated typhoid empirically with a carbapenem. XDR Typhi (resistant to ampicillin, ceftriaxone, chloramphenicol, ciprofloxacin, TMP/SMX) is typically susceptible to azithromycin and carbapenems. XDR not improving on a carbapenem alone might benefit from adding a second antibiotic (eg, azithromycin) (case reports)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Parenteral bactericidal beta-lactams with an extremely broad spectrum."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Seizures and other CNS effects, mostly with CNS disorders, meningitis or renal impairment (imipenem not used in meningitis for seizure risk). C. difficile diarrhea."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hypersensitivity to carbapenems or prior anaphylaxis to beta-lactams. Pregnancy: only when safer antibiotics aren't an option."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lowers valproic acid levels:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " risk of breakthrough seizures."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
